==============================================================================
S1  MDE for the paired per-time-point contrast (n = 4 pairs)
==============================================================================
design: 28 pairs, 4 replicates per role x time point, times = [3.0, 6.0, 9.0, 12.0, 15.0, 18.0, 21.0]
formula (closed form): MDE = (t_crit + t_beta) * SD / sqrt(n)
formula (exact)      : solve delta such that power(delta) = P(T' > t_crit | df=n-1, ncp=delta*sqrt(n)/SD) + P(T' < -t_crit | df=n-1, ncp=delta*sqrt(n)/SD) = 0.80
   t=    3  diff = -0.517 pp  SD =   5.3258  MDE(closed) =  11.0800 pp  MDE(nct) =  11.3330 pp  paired t = -0.194 (p = 0.8585)
   t=    6  diff = -0.522 pp  SD =   5.7810  MDE(closed) =  12.0270 pp  MDE(nct) =  12.3016 pp  paired t = -0.181 (p = 0.8683)
   t=    9  diff = +0.996 pp  SD =   5.4368  MDE(closed) =  11.3110 pp  MDE(nct) =  11.5692 pp  paired t = +0.366 (p = 0.7385)
   t=   12  diff = -1.083 pp  SD =   9.9782  MDE(closed) =  20.7592 pp  MDE(nct) =  21.2331 pp  paired t = -0.217 (p = 0.8421)
   t=   15  diff = +0.196 pp  SD =  10.9109  MDE(closed) =  22.6998 pp  MDE(nct) =  23.2179 pp  paired t = +0.036 (p = 0.9736)
   t=   18  diff = -2.382 pp  SD =   6.3228  MDE(closed) =  13.1543 pp  MDE(nct) =  13.4545 pp  paired t = -0.754 (p = 0.5059)
   t=   21  diff = -3.057 pp  SD =   8.3255  MDE(closed) =  17.3208 pp  MDE(nct) =  17.7162 pp  paired t = -0.734 (p = 0.5159)

   observed paired SD: median = 6.3228 pp; pooled RMS = 7.7390 pp (sqrt of the mean of the 7 per-time-point variances)
   MDE computed from the pooled SD: 16.1007 pp
   median MDE across the 7 time points: closed form = 13.1543 pp; noncentral t = 13.4545 pp (noncentral-t inversion available for 7/7 time points)
   MDE range: 11.0800 to 22.6998 pp
   time points whose MDE is at or below 3 pp: 0/7

   STATEMENT: differences smaller than 13.15 pp (median MDE; range 11.08-22.70 pp) could not have been detected by this paired design at 80% power and alpha = 0.05 two-sided with n = 4 pairs.

   late-time contrast t=21: observed difference = -3.057 pp against an MDE of 17.321 pp -> observed effect is INSIDE (below) the resolution floor
   power of the t=21 test at the observed effect size: 0.0830

==============================================================================
S2  TOST equivalence at each time point
==============================================================================
formula: two one-sided t tests at alpha each: p_lower = P(T_{n-1} >= (mean - low)/SE), p_upper = P(T_{n-1} <= (mean - high)/SE); TOST p = max(p_lower, p_upper); equivalence declared iff TOST p < alpha (equivalently the 90% CI lies inside [-margin, +margin])
margins reported: (i) margin = observed paired SD at that time point
  (margin = one SD, derived from the data), (ii) margin = 3 pp (fixed scale).
   t=    3  diff = -0.517 pp  90% CI [-8.991, +7.958] (half-width 8.474)
          margin = 1 SD (5.326 pp): TOST p = 0.0843 equivalent = False   | margin = 3 pp: TOST p = 0.2099 equivalent = False
   t=    6  diff = -0.522 pp  90% CI [-9.721, +8.677] (half-width 9.199)
          margin = 1 SD (5.781 pp): TOST p = 0.0832 equivalent = False   | margin = 3 pp: TOST p = 0.2271 equivalent = False
   t=    9  diff = +0.996 pp  90% CI [-7.655, +9.647] (half-width 8.651)
          margin = 1 SD (5.437 pp): TOST p = 0.1004 equivalent = False   | margin = 3 pp: TOST p = 0.2572 equivalent = False
   t=   12  diff = -1.083 pp  90% CI [-16.960, +14.795] (half-width 15.878)
          margin = 1 SD (9.978 pp): TOST p = 0.0863 equivalent = False   | margin = 3 pp: TOST p = 0.3632 equivalent = False
   t=   15  diff = +0.196 pp  90% CI [-17.166, +17.558] (half-width 17.362)
          margin = 1 SD (10.911 pp): TOST p = 0.0721 equivalent = False   | margin = 3 pp: TOST p = 0.3214 equivalent = False
   t=   18  diff = -2.382 pp  90% CI [-12.443, +7.679] (half-width 10.061)
          margin = 1 SD (6.323 pp): TOST p = 0.1505 equivalent = False   | margin = 3 pp: TOST p = 0.4288 equivalent = False
   t=   21  diff = -3.057 pp  90% CI [-16.305, +10.190] (half-width 13.248)
          margin = 1 SD (8.325 pp): TOST p = 0.1475 equivalent = False   | margin = 3 pp: TOST p = 0.5051 equivalent = False

   equivalent within the 1-SD margin at 0/7 time points; equivalent within the +/-3 pp margin at 0/7 time points
   smallest TOST p: 0.0721 (1-SD margin), 0.2099 (3 pp margin)
   structural reason for the 1-SD margin: with n = 4 the 90% CI half-width is t(.95,3)*SD/2 = 1.1767 * SD > 1 * SD, so the CI can never fit inside a one-SD margin - equivalence within one SD is unreachable by construction at this n.
   INTERPRETATION: failing to declare equivalence is NOT evidence of a difference. Every paired t is non-significant (all p >= 0.506); the design is too imprecise to certify either a difference or equivalence at any margin at or below one SD / 3 pp.

==============================================================================
S3  Assays needed for the compartment fold-change ordering to reach p < 0.05
==============================================================================
formula: S_obs(k) = W_obs * k^2 * (m^3 - m) / 12; required k = smallest k with S_obs(k) >= S_crit(k), where S_crit(k) is the permutation-null 5% critical value for k raters on m items
exact permutation null table built for k = 2..60, m = 3 (5.55 s); S_crit(k=3) = 18.0, S_crit(k=5) = 32.0, S_crit(k=27) = 162.0, chi2-approx S_crit(k=3) = 17.97

   endpoint_count: observed W = 0.7778 (S = 14.0, chi2 = 4.6667, p_chi2 = 0.0970, exact p = 0.194444)
      observed per-assay rank vectors (1 = lowest fold change): assay_1:(3, 2, 1); assay_2:(3, 1, 2); assay_3:(3, 2, 1)
      exact p at perfect concordance (W = 1, k = 3): 0.027778
      assays needed, chi-square approximation: 4 (p there = 0.0446)
      assays needed, exact permutation null: 5 (p there = 0.0085)
      bootstrap over observed orderings (2000 draws, cap k = 40): min = 3, median = 4.0, p90 = 5.0, cap not reached in 0/2000 draws

   endpoint_fraction: observed W = 0.1111 (S = 2.0, chi2 = 0.6667, p_chi2 = 0.7165, exact p = 0.944444)
      observed per-assay rank vectors (1 = lowest fold change): assay_1:(3, 1, 2); assay_2:(3, 2, 1); assay_3:(1, 2, 3)
      exact p at perfect concordance (W = 1, k = 3): 0.027778
      assays needed, chi-square approximation: 27 (p there = 0.0498)
      assays needed, exact permutation null: 27 (p there = 0.0478)
      bootstrap over observed orderings (2000 draws, cap k = 40): min = 3, median = 14.0, p90 = 32.0, cap not reached in 198/2000 draws

