==============================================================================
S5  Within-cell replicate resolution of log2 fold change (compartment file)
==============================================================================
formula: MDE_pair = q_crit(0.05, k_groups, df_error) * SD_within / sqrt(n_per_group)
   design: 18 cells, 4 replicates per cell, df_within = 54
   within-cell SD of log2 fold change: pooled RMS = 0.7107 log2 units, median = 0.6836 (range 0.1471 - 1.2027)
   -> geometric SD of the per-replicate fold change = 2^0.7107 = 1.6366x
   chi-square 95% CI on that SD (df = 54): 0.5983 - 0.8755
   MDE between two compartment means, Tukey-style (k = 3 groups, n = 4, df_error = 6): q * SD / sqrt(n) = 4.3392 * 0.7107 / 2.0000 = 1.5420 log2 (= 2.9119x fold-change ratio)
   MDE between two compartment means, two-sample t (df = 6): 1.6849 log2 (= 3.2151x)
   MDE between two compartment means, Tukey with pooled df = 54: 1.2111 log2 (= 2.3152x); two-sample t with df = 54: 1.4339 log2 (= 2.7017x)
   MDE if the same biological replicate could be paired across compartments (upper bound using SD_gap = sqrt(2)*SD_within): 2.0911 log2 (= 4.2607x)
   observed compartment-level log2FC spread (core analysis): compartment_1 = 1.0386, compartment_2 = 0.8137, compartment_3 = 0.7596; span = 0.2790 log2 = 1.2134x
   -> the reliable floor (1.542 log2 = 2.912x) is much larger than the entire observed compartment span (0.279 log2 = 1.213x); every bottom-two ordering gap from the core results (0.0048 - 0.3370 log2) is far below that floor, so the ordering is being read off differences the per-cell replicates cannot resolve
